# Curated distribution allowlist — the ONLY files that ship to the team harness repo.
# One path per line; a trailing "/" copies a directory recursively. Blank lines and
# lines starting with "#" are ignored. Anything not listed here stays private in the
# source repo (proposals, HANDOFF, DISTRIBUTION, preview.html, storybook internals, …).
# build-dist.mjs also GENERATES: README.md (consumer) + CHANGELOG.md (released versions only).

# --- The contract + specs (English; Korean is on-demand in the hub, not shipped) ---
design.md
foundations.md
components.md
recipes.md
patterns.md
ai-patterns.md
content.md
icons.md

# --- Tokens + machine index (load-first for agents) ---
tokens/synapse.tokens.json
tokens/synapse.css
tokens/fonts.css
synapse.manifest.json
# NB: assets/fonts/ is intentionally NOT shipped — Artific is licensed to Enhans and
# must not be redistributed in the public harness (see foundations.md §2.1 / assets/fonts/README.md).

# --- Enforcement tools (stdlib-only Python; the gate SHIPS WITH the contract —
# a harness that references validate.py must contain validate.py) ---
tools/validate.py
tools/synapse.py
tools/build_manifest.py
tools/check_icons.py
tools/screen-intent.schema.json
examples/screen-intent.example.json
# check_icons.py hard-requires the icon registry at import; the registry is generated
# from the pinned ISC-licensed lucide-static package, so unlike assets/fonts/ it may ship.
assets/icons/lucide-registry.json

# --- Generation prompt + team workflow ---
docs/process/prd-template.md
docs/process/design-review-protocol.md
# The review protocol's feedback loop: the fill-in PR template captures the
# correction-ledger block, and the ledger doc defines its closed vocabulary
# (synapse.py digest parses that format).
.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/ui_review.md
docs/process/correction-ledger.md
tooling/product-gates/

# --- App Generation feature: chart/component catalog (reconciled to v1.0.0) ---
app-generation/

# --- Product migration: the conversion guides (one per area) + their index ---
# Listed INDIVIDUALLY, never as `migration/`: the rest of that folder is the pre-1.0
# shadcn migration's working papers (color-token-map.*, component-inventory-diff.md,
# decisions.md, replacement-rules.*, token-*.md, variant-decisions.md, the review CSVs
# and generated HTML dumps, verify-token-map.py) — a finished internal audit trail that
# names rejected options and must stay private. migration/README.md is the two-part index
# that keeps the next person from shipping the wrong half.
migration/README.md
migration/2026-08-06-audit-migration-guide.md
migration/color-token-snapping.md
migration/scale-snapping.md
migration/typography-tailwind-migration.md
migration/icon-sizing.md
migration/shadow-triage.md
migration/motion-durations.md
migration/z-index-migration.md
